WEBVTT

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>The finish line...</i>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.070
<i>Soon someone will be crowned</i>

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.070
<i>the winner of the Inter-High's second day.</i>

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.740
<i>It's the last few meters.</i>

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.370
<i>But it's the hardest few meters of all.</i>

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.370
<i>You can do it, Imaizumi-kun!</i>

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.930
<i>You can go faster, Imaizumi Shunsuke!</i>

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.170
<i>Surpass your limits!</i>

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:28.900
<i>You just watch.</i>

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.790
<i>I can't give up after carrying the 
jersey entrusted to me this far!</i>

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.930
<i>I'll jam it across the finish line first!</i>

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:43.730
<i>Until I do, I can't stop pumping
these legs, even if they fall to pieces!</i>

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.310
Move, Shinkai!

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.100
That's my spot!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.170
<i>More! This is the end!</i>

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.320
<i>Grant me your strength!</i>

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.080
<i>Naruko, give me your determination!</i>

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.990
<i>Onoda, give me your unwavering effort!</i>

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.080
There's thirty meters to the finish line!

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.090
<i>I'll hold my position!</i>

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.570
<i>Go all out, Imaizumi Shunsuke!</i>

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.370
<i>I won't let you!</i>

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.710
Morphokya!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.960
<i>Friendship! Determination! Trust! Bonds!</i>

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.010
<i>They're all trash!</i>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.050
<i>All you need is desire!</i>

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.890
<i>All that matters is how much you want it!</i>

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.100
<i>Victory...</i>

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.660
<i>Winning...</i>

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:28.660
<i>All that matters is how 
desperate you are to taste it!</i>

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.110
<i>You don't need any roundabout reasons to win!</i>

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>It only matters if you're 
so desperate to win,</i>

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.030
<i>you sprout arms from every pore on your body!</i>

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.450
<i>If you need it that badly!</i>

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.760
What's with the Kyoto Fushimi
 guy's strange aura?

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.000
It's insane!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.500
Twenty meters remain!
All three are charging ahead!

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.000
It's the finish line!

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:06.520
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:30.040
<i>LINE.23  Winner</i>

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.260
<i>Victory!</i>

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:29.880
<i>The finish line!</i>

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.140
<i>It's right there!</i>

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:33.350
<i>Dive in!</i>

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.940
<i>Imaizumi Shunsuke!</i>

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.690
<i>To the finish line before you!</i>

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.780
<i>Win!</i>

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.280
<i>I'll win!</i>

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.880
<i>Ashikiba-san!</i>

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.160
<i>I'll win the finish line 
sprint you told me to take!</i>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>Only forward!</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>Forward, forward!</i>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.080
<i>That's all!</i>

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.090
Go, Imaizumi!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.210
You can do it!

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.090
Imaizumi-san!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.090
Imaizumi-kun!

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.460
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.840
<i>I'll win!</i>

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.720
<i>Give up everything!</i>

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.470
Yeah!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.490
Phokyaaa!

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.820
<i>For this finish line!</i>

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.530
<b>Hakone</b>

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.990
<i>Winning a road race</i>

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:30.260
<i>that involves riding one hundred, sometimes
 two hundred kilometers in a single day</i>

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.500
<i>means you overcame obstacles, 
had luck on your side,</i>

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.550
<i>prepared and devised strategies,</i>

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.750
<i>and finished the race with a strong will.</i>

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.010
<i>That's why everyone showers you with praise.</i>

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.260
<i>They're generous with their applause.</i>

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.380
Who won?

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.810
They finished nearly simultaneously!

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.820
<i>We have the results of 
the finish line sprint.</i>

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.990
<i>It was very close, but the winner 
of the Inter-High's second day is...</i>

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:13.160
<i>Kyoto Fushimi High School's #111, 
second-year Midousuji Akira!</i>

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.370
Won... I won...

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:22.760
Victory, victory, victory, victory!

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.610
I won this time.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:31.720
I kept it from escaping, like a firefly.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:35.350
He beat Hakone Academy and Sohoku!

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:38.350
Who called him gross during the race?

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.360
He's awesome!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.800
<i>A delightful finish! Ultimate victory!</i>

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.880
<i>Gaze upon me!</i>

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.030
<i>This... This is...</i>

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:57.540
<i>Today's strongest man, Midousuji Akira-kun!</i>

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.130
What's gotten into him?

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.040
Maybe it's a victory pose...

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.510
I've never seen anything like it!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.550
He's waving his arms?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.440
There's nothing normal about him.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.520
I'm a fan now!

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.220
Me, too!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.100
Midousuji!

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.250
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.180
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.180
Midousuji!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.410
<i>Surge! Tremble!</i>

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.440
<i>Shake and delight!</i>

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.480
<i>Yes, me!</i>

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.840
<i>I'm the man who won everything!</i>

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.690
<i>Who overthrew everything!</i>

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.990
<i>Midousuji Akira-kun!</i>

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.950
<i>The sole victor of today's race!</i>

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.540
<i>With some delay, Hakone Academy's Ashikiba 
crosses the finish line in fourth!</i>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.330
<i>The fifth place racer is entering 
the final straightaway!</i>

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.880
<i>Midousuji-kun just barely 
won the finish line sprint.</i>

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.130
<i>Imaizumi-kun...</i>

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:54.300
<i>The atmosphere of the crowd feels strange.</i>

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.850
<i>The air feels heavy.</i>

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.570
<i>They're all excited.</i>

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:02.600
<i>The crowd's focus is directed 
toward Midousuji-kun's victory.</i>

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.110
<i>They probably expected Hakone Academy to win.</i>

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.950
<i>Since he overcame that,
they're intoxicated by the upset.</i>

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.490
<i>This is what we did last year.</i>

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.660
<i>The pressure is incredible.</i>

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.230
Last year's dark horse was Sohoku!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:21.450
And then Hakone Academy beat them yesterday!

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.040
Maybe this year's dark horse 
will be Kyoto Fushimi!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.300
<i>What?</i>

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.050
<i>Someone's coming?</i>

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.920
<i>There's 300 meters left. That's...</i>

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.690
<i>Kyoto Fushimi #112, Captain Mizuta-san!</i>

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:38.340
I heard them announce our team's victory!

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.890
Victory for Kyoto Fushimi, 
the team I'm the captain of!

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.060
The news restored my energy!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.470
I'm passing the Mountain King!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.200
Listen closely, Onoda.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.340
The Inter-High uses special rules.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.760
We start in the order we finish.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:58.100
That day's results affect 
the next day's race.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.340
Try to finish as quickly as possible.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.170
If you end up racing someone at the 
finish line, don't let them win.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.520
Mizuta!

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.440
Mizuta!

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:05.960
Onoda-kun!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.400
Wow! Kyoto Fushimi, go!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.840
He passed Sohoku's #1!

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.780
<i>It's a come-from-behind victory!</i>

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.590
<i>Kyoto Fushimi's Captain 
Mizuta Nobuyuki takes fifth!</i>

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.340
Midousuji-kun, could we get a comment?

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.430
Did things go as planned?

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:35.160
<i>Riders are crossing one after another 
at the Lake Haruna finish line!</i>

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.410
<b>Chiba
Sohoku High School</b>

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.650
I'm sorry!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:57.140
Because I couldn't stay ahead in the last 
few centimeters, we lost to Kyoto Fushimi.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:01.590
Imaizumi-kun, you don't 
need to apologize so—

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.720
Imaizumi...

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.850
I'm sorry.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.910
I have no excuse.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:12.200
I attacked with 250 meters remaining 
and threw my bike at the end,

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.860
but I failed to reach the finish line.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.470
It's because I wasn't strong enough!

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.860
I wasn't good enough!

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.040
Taking the finish line is the ace's job.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.250
All of us, including Naruko,

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.750
rode all out for the finish line.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.890
We trusted you.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.930
You failed to do your job.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.130
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.160
That's the logic, anyway.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.850
But the ace can't win every time.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.020
We fully trusted you.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.170
You rode as hard as you could.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.860
If you still couldn't win, then so it goes.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.740
But we don't know if
 I rode as hard as I could!

00:09:56.440 --> 00:10:00.660
Sugimoto told me all about 
how hard you worked.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.770
He said it was the best you've ever ridden.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.410
That you rode powerfully.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:10.420
In the end, he broke down in tears.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:15.960
If it was enough to make him cry, the way
 you rode could be nothing if not all out.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.270
Right?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.690
The results are disappointing,

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:24.930
but we should feel relieved that everyone 
survived and finished in one piece.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.100
<i>Sugimoto...</i>

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.390
There's still tomorrow.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.970
We have another chance.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.390
Uh, you know what they say.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:38.940
"Go to hell."

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.850
Rise up from the depths of hell.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:45.420
You just told him to go to hell.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.830
Seriously?

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.210
<i>Naruko...</i>

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:51.880
You're weak.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.080
Show off, show off, and show off...

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.530
Show off until you can't anymore.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:01.650
The hotshot I know is cooler 
and haughtier than this.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.150
The second day was exhausting!

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.430
It was hard.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.980
It was a long stage.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.590
It really was a close race for the finish.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:15.730
If you thought so, then it must've been.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.640
<i>Naruko.</i>

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:22.420
Winners, please come to the stage.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.950
I suppose I should take my place

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:31.370
at the highest point on the winner's podium.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.730
The winner of the Inter-High's 
second day is Kyoto Fushimi's ace,

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.920
#111, Midousuji Akira!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.690
He will receive a bouquet of flowers 
and the winner's yellow number tag

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:47.310
to wear while riding tomorrow!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.610
Let's ask him how he's feeling right now.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:56.580
Hello, everyone.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:59.110
My name is Midousuji Akira.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.920
He's a funny guy.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:01.860
He said hello.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:07.120
I have one thing to say about today's race.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:08.700
Gross!

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.000
Huh?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.200
Oh, excuse me.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.210
There was something wrong with the mic.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:20.670
Today I was involved in a 
very close race at the end.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.620
I was able to keep racing until 
the end because of the fans,

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.180
my teammates, the support staff, and...

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:32.140
Because I had these two strong, strong rivals.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:34.810
Because I had rivals.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.020
They're lizards.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.050
Li...

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.440
Did he say lizards?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:45.940
Like lizards that crawl around and 
are quick to hide under rocks.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:53.160
Because these imbeciles on either side 
of me rode without courage or strength...

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.460
I was able to win.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.380
Gross!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:04.380
Gross, gross, gross, gross, 
gross, gross, gross, gross!

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.050
What's wrong?

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:10.210
You look nonchalant. And you look so formal.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:13.390
You look like you're not frustrated.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:15.890
Your fans are disappointed.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.650
You've got to show them a 
greater variety of expressions.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.570
Are you trying to show off?

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.810
Aren't you actually 
seething with frustration?

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:28.790
Don't you wish you could do it 
over if you had a time machine?

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:31.430
But too bad!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.210
You lost!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:39.750
There's no price you can 
pay to change the results!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.660
They just barely lost.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:47.510
But in road racing, it doesn't 
matter how close you were.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.830
It's not the difference, but the rank!

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:53.320
One kilometer, ten kilometers,
a few centimeters... It's all the same!

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.520
Road racing is win or lose!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:00.560
Topography! Strategy! Resourcefulness! 
Will! Strength! Decision-making ability!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:07.590
In every way, I was far 
superior to these pests!

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:13.290
I proved that of all the
 people who raced today,

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.620
I was the most right!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.650
No, he's right.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.900
Winning proves that.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:24.850
He's so unconventional!

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:26.460
He's overcome Hakone Academy!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:28.150
The champs have been replaced.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.290
No, he's not a champion.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.650
He's a ruler!

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:37.530
He beat back Hakone Academy's steady advance 
and beat last year's winners, Sohoku!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:39.060
All by himself, too!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.560
He's the ruler of the race, Midousuji Akira!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.450
Midousuji!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.820
Kyoto Fushimi!

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:47.910
<i>People are weak.</i>

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.490
<i>That's why they look up to the strong.</i>

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:58.000
<i>With a victorious cry,
I swayed the crowd to my side.</i>

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.730
<i>Tomorrow is the last day.</i>

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:04.500
<i>Tomorrow's race should 
be even more interesting.</i>

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:08.260
The sprint and mountain awards 
will be handed out next.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.640
Loss, huh?

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.700
Either way, tomorrow is our last race.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:19.450
We'll have to face off against 
the guys standing on that stage.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.230
Yeah.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:25.980
And it'll be our last race together, Hajime.

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:29.740
We third-years are retiring after this race.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.820
Yeah, Junta.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.800
Will you keep me from trembling tomorrow, too?

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.670
Yeah, I will.

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.240
You will pull me across the flats?

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.960
Yeah, I'll pull you at 100% speed.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.960
That's good to hear.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.490
You know, I've been thinking...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.960
I have a small wish.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.560
I'm hoping that during tomorrow's 
race at the Inter-High,

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:57.470
we can sync up our movements and breathing

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.480
and do our Synchronized Straight Twin.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.530
I'm okay. It's nothing.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.920
I just tripped.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.640
I'm tired from today's race.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.580
I'll be fine after some rest.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.540
You're doing more laundry, Miki?

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.890
Yeah. I just have this and 
this and this, Aya-chan.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.920
Why are you smiling?

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:38.260
<i>I never thought I was doing 
it alone, but I was arrogant.</i>

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.770
<i>I thought I just had to do my best.</i>

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.650
<i>That he would help me.</i>

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.010
<i>Somewhere in my mind, I thought that.</i>

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:52.530
<i>I hid behind my weakness.</i>

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:56.030
<i>Like he has until now.</i>

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.990
<i>Like he did today.</i>

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.700
<i>I thought he'd do something.</i>

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:06.440
<i>I'm an idiot. I relied on him too much.</i>

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.070
<i>I assumed he was tough.</i>

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:10.750
<i>I assumed he'd always be by my side.</i>

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.670
I'm okay. It's nothing.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.090
<i>Of course it's not "nothing"!</i>

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.970
<i>But I told him my dream.</i>

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.740
<i>Aoyagi, are you hurting?</i>

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.450
<i>What about tomorrow's race?</i>

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.410
<i>Junta...</i>

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:40.870
<i>Thanks for telling me your dream.</i>

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:45.000
<i>I always worry about the 
things I couldn't do.</i>

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.050
<i>That's why your cheerfulness saves me.</i>

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.010
<i>You always tell me about 
miracles, hopes, and dreams.</i>

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:55.950
<i>Because of the visions you show me,</i>

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:59.720
<i>I'm able to move forward, Junta.</i>

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.220
<i>I pushed myself too hard.</i>

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.480
<i>The pain's getting worse.</i>

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.720
<i>I don't have a choice.</i>

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.210
<i>I'll have to rely on someone.</i>

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.290
<i>An experienced first-year...</i>

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:15.360
<i>Kaburagi? No...</i>

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.570
What? You're injured?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:20.750
Danchiku, I'm going to ride tomorrow.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.160
So I need you to get some things for me.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:23.910
Yes, sir.

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:29.580
All the tape, supports, ice, 
and painkillers we have.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.820
I need you to tape me up 
and massage me in my room.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:37.170
And don't tell anyone about this.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.300
Not even Kaburagi.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:41.270
We don't need to make them worry.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.300
Yes, sir.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.290
What are you up to, Onoda-kun?

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:47.920
Naruko-kun.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.170
You're riding after your bath?

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.650
Yeah.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:56.270
Toji-san swapped my gears out for some 
lighter climbing ones for tomorrow's race.

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:59.240
I thought I'd test them out.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.450
Really?

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:02.580
But that's not the only reason.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:06.580
Tomorrow's the last day 
of this year's Inter-High.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:09.640
When I think about it, I can't relax.

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:12.640
I feel excited and restless.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:15.300
I feel like I still have things left undone.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.460
I thought riding my bike would help me relax.

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:22.750
Sounds like you.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:30.710
But what sounds even more like you is 
listening to a Whatever Hime CD on repeat.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:33.730
<b>Love Hime</b>

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.500
That would work, too!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.730
Which should I do?

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.530
You've already got your bike out.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.890
Go for a ride.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.530
Okay. I'll be back soon.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.060
<i>I'm nervous.</i>

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>Tomorrow's the last race.</i>

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:51.550
<i>Everyone's done their best this past year.</i>

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.330
<i>They've worked really hard.</i>

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:55.340
<i>But as of right now,</i>

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:59.760
<i>Sohoku hasn't won a single 
number tag at this Inter-High.</i>

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:05.170
<i>Imaizumi-kun did his best at the 
finish line today, but he didn't win.</i>

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:08.100
<i>Tomorrow's the last day.</i>

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.270
<i>I have to work hard on the third day.</i>

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:15.780
<i>Since I won last year, they probably 
expect me to win this year.</i>

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.230
<i>I wonder if I can.</i>

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:21.130
No, I shouldn't think that!

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.740
I won't be able to relax!

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:28.240
But last year, I had Makishima-san.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.330
Enjoy the tension for now.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.870
They're motivating us 
more than you might expect.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.420
You have to think of ways

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.790
to turn the situation around.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.180
No, what am I thinking?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:44.720
Aoyagi-san said it's different this year.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:45.890
I'm stronger now.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:49.300
I'll sing the <i>Love Hime</i> song.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:55.400
I've always felt these hidden feelings—

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.750
<i>Huh? A bike?</i>

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:01.150
<i>Who's riding this late at 
night on this narrow pass?</i>

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.650
<i>I've seen that form before.</i>

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.360
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.280
<i>And silent.</i>

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:14.360
<i>He's climbing silently, like he's on rails.</i>

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:17.290
<i>So quietly that it puts 
even the forest to sleep.</i>

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.380
<i>The Sleeping Climb!</i>

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.040
<i>It must be him.</i>

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.470
<i>The man who brought excitement to the 
mountains at last year's Inter-High...</i>

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.970
Hakone Academy's Mountain God, Toudou-san!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.810
Well, if isn't four-eyes.

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:04.790
Princess, Princess!

00:23:04.790 --> 00:23:06.640
I love, love, love you!

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:08.200
Princess! Princess!

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.240
Hearing this song gives me strength.

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:09.560
Twinkle, twinkle!

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:12.170
Jeez! Please don't sing that song!

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:13.990
You're not going to sing?

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:15.680
No way!

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:18.200
I had no choice before, when it
 was a command from God...

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:20.210
Teshima-san, please put a stop to this!

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:21.370
Princess, Princess!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:22.940
Hey!

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:24.060
Princess, Princess...

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:25.170
Danchiku...

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:27.750
Today, we'll sing the medley!

00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:32.090
I've always felt these hidden feelings!

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.050
You'll always be my princess!

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:34.050
Huh?

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.180
Ta-ta-ta-tan!

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:36.230
What?!

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  The Small Pass</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.250
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
